codex
The local-rule review confirms the main limitation is not program substitution: fixed semantics proves explicit results for empty, three-, and four-element witnesses. The candidate’s loop bridge preserves a tested continuation, but it broadens its proved premise (`builtinsScope` becomes arbitrary `BS`) and leaves ground outputs as uninterpreted `strangePrefix` values. I found a concrete out-of-entry-context witness where fixed execution is stuck on missing `len` while the bridge proves termination; the actual entry claim itself fixes `builtinsScope`, so I’m recording this as an over-broad bridge/evidence gap unless a false entry-domain conclusion emerges.
